{"chunk_id": "2502516f874a", "text": "In the raging climax of the battle, Ravana launches a blazing, bell\u2011ringing spear at Rama. Rama counters with arrows, but the titan\u2019s weapon burns through them until Rama hurls a divine spear brought by Matali and favored by Indra. The clash shatters Ravana\u2019s lance, and Rama wounds Ravana\u2019s horses and body with a storm of arrows, leaving the demon king bleeding like a flowering ashoka tree. Ravana retaliates with a deluge of shafts, and the two heroes darken the battlefield with their missiles. Amid the fury, Rama openly condemns Ravana for abducting Sita like a thief and coward, declaring that the act has invited death upon him. The scene combines ferocious combat with moral accusation, framing the battle as both physical duel and righteous judgment.\nRama and Ravana exchange devastating volleys of weapons before Rama condemns Ravana for abducting Sita and vows his imminent death.\nThemes: heroic combat, righteous condemnation, honor and cowardice, revenge for Sita, divine weaponry", "vector": [-0.017619838938117027, -0.025197833776474, -0.0043217213824391365, 0.020230185240507126, -0.010967450216412544, 0.01900492049753666, -0.0409930944442749, -0.017686428502202034, -0.025357650592923164, -0.029273170977830887, 0.019657505676150322, 0.02722218446433544, 0.009855389595031738, 0.007764448877424002, -0.0032346320804208517, 0.009023008868098259, 0.03598548844456673, -0.008916463702917099, 0.024838244542479515, -0.016767479479312897, -0.008363762870430946, -0.006738955620676279, -0.014010634273290634, 0.030738160014152527, -0.031004521995782852, -0.004997614771127701, 0.024238931015133858, -0.03856920078396797, 0.022454306483268738, -0.005626894533634186, -0.014836356975138187, -0.015302489511668682, -0.001551557914353907, -0.004298414569348097, -0.01871192269027233, 0.011047358624637127, -0.000899803708307445, -0.009708890691399574, 0.006825522985309362, 0.00535720307379961, 0.002059310209006071, -0.0099419569